From 17fd0c5954143f650307305f53a3d25b91320e69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eldin Lee <eldin.lee@quantatw.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 23:04:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] meta: add Ventura2 network initialization support

Add support for Meta Ventura2 platform initialization.

The Ventura2 platform uses a Marvell 88E6393X switch and
88E1512 PHYs. Add the required initialization sequence to
configure the switch, PHYs, SERDES links, and LED settings.

Add a userspace MDIO netlink wrapper for accessing the
native ASPEED MDIO controller and an FTDI MPSSE-based
Clause 22 MDIO implementation.

Add an MDIO backend abstraction layer that automatically
selects between the native MDIO and FTDI-based
implementations at runtime.

Extend the FTDI-based MDIO backend to support both
AST2600 and AST2700 platforms by probing the appropriate
USB controller instance during initialization.

Add Meson wrap definitions for libusb, libmnl and libftdi1 to
support dependency fallback during CI builds when the
required development packages are not available in the
build environment.

Update Meson build rules and dependencies required by the
new platform support.

Depends-on:
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/92583

Change-Id: Ic4a3e9d2faba4666bdf95fe512cc4f522f6eb2a1
Signed-off-by: Eldin Lee <eldin.lee@quantatw.com>
